            <p class="ts-hdive__lead">Any digital camera and a light source that can give you red, green and blue separately. Monochrome sensors gain the most, since there is no colour filter array in the way at all.</p>
            <p class="ts-hdive__lead">A companion web app that turns your phone into the light source is on the way, so you will be able to try RGB with nothing more than the screen in your pocket.</p>
            <a class="ts-hdive__link" href="#signup">Try it in the beta <span aria-hidden="true">›</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} the detail: how channel separation works and why it beats one white shot.
