              <p class="ts-rgbcard__d">Instead of one exposure under white light, the frame is photographed three times: once under red, once under green, once under blue. Each exposure reads one dye layer of the negative more or less on its own. toneScan Studio spots the three frames sitting in your capture folder, groups them into a triplet and combines them, with per-channel exposure targets so no channel lands under-exposed and crosstalk correction measured from your own setup.</p>
